In the game I saw you have done a couple of mistakes with the
E-word; one already mentioned, the other was to engrave more
than one word while monsters were adjacent. Always add just a
single one.

Another misconception is visible in what you wrote above. Use
the E-word as a means to scare the monsters, then try to escape.
But don't try to heal yourself. As you observed it takes too
much time, and in the meantime new monsters get spawned, and
amongst them there can be monsters that shoot missiles and zap
wands at you. (This said for "writing in the dust"; it's a
different issue when you have something more reliable that's
applicable in a single turn.)

